{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Reduce rebar tickets-store growth and reclaim the ~1 GiB already spent, by making the\nreconciler's committed `.bridge_state` cache cheap instead of re-homing it.\n\nMeasured facts, full research trail and the three corrected false premises: session_log\n**1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (dinky-frowsy-woodborer). Supersedes the tabled plan in\n**bronze-used-foxhound** (e594-e1d0). Umbrella: **1270-b740**.\n\n## Context\n\nThe `tickets` branch is **1.04 GiB**; **92%** is the reconciler's `.bridge_state` cache, not\nticket data (events are 55 MB). Diffing consecutive committed revisions of `bindings.json`\n(1509 bindings) shows the growth is bookkeeping nothing reads:\n\n| field | entries changed per pass |\n|---|---|\n| `baseline` (the value) | **0** |\n| `baseline_advanced_at` (written at `binding_store.py:375`, read nowhere in `src/`) | **1144** |\n| `last_get_pass` (rotation bookkeeping) | **20** |\n\nA scattered edit across a sort-ordered 18 MB file defeats git delta compression. Measured on 40\nconsecutive real revisions rebuilt in a clean repo and repacked `--window=250 --depth=50`, true\nmarginal cost per version is **12.79 KB** today, **1.74 KB** after deleting the timestamp (7.4x),\nand the version count halves once rotation bookkeeping moves out (12.8x total).\n\n## Approach and why this one\n\nKeep the cache committed and make it cheap. `.bridge_state` must stay on-branch because the\nreconciler runs on **ephemeral** GitHub-hosted runners, so durable state has to live in git. An\nearlier design wrote prev to the main-branch worktree, so prev was always `{}` and the differ\nre-derived 2050+ inbound creates every pass (`reconcile.py:258-259`). Epic `6c9c` evaluated and\ndropped re-homing it off-branch because the convergence loop already self-heals binding drift.\nThe levers are content and churn, not location.\n\nThe one-time reclaim of existing history is included under an operator-approved quiescence\nprotocol. Its mechanics are proven: a length-aware\n`git fast-export --no-data | filter | git fast-import` pipeline on the real branch produced\n1,172,586,762 -> 98,803,422 bytes (8.4%) while preserving all 49,888 commits and 2,661 merges.\nThe dynamic re-add restores the current `.bridge_state` files, so the rewritten HEAD tree is\n**exactly byte-identical** to the recorded pre-rewrite tip tree; only historical versions of the\ntarget paths are removed. Stock git plumbing is used because it is already available and proven\nfor this repository, avoiding a new third-party core dependency. `git-filter-repo` could preserve\nempty commits with `--prune-empty=never`; DAG preservation is therefore not a reason to reject it.\n\n## Scope (children, in dependency order)\n\n1. **A1** delete `baseline_advanced_at` and add the write-when-changed guard in `set_baseline`.\n2. **A4-1** fence `bridge_fsck` before `prev_snapshot.json` is narrowed (independent of A1).\n3. **A2-1** move `last_get_pass` to `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json`; write both formats and\n   read `max(new, legacy)`.\n4. **A3** text-normalize baseline description/status/priority, deliberately excluding assignee.\n5. **A2-2** delete the legacy inline `last_get_pass` field only after its rollout gate clears.\n6. **A4-2** narrow `prev_snapshot.json` to a key-set after A4-1; record forward and reverse corpus\n   mutation diffs before merge.\n7. **A4-3** suppress branch-3 mutations whose effective Jira payload is empty.\n8. **A5** record all committed-format changes, mixed-version rules, and rollback boundaries in\n   an ADR after A3 and A4-2 establish the final shapes.\n9. **A6-0a** add the fail-closed store-epoch guard at both union sites after A2-2 and A4-3.\n10. **A6-0b** make the persistent review-bot clone self-converge and fix its deploy trigger; it\n    ships with A6-0a so an `src/rebar/` change activates the deploy path.\n11. **A6-0c** build and dry-run the stock-git history-strip tooling after A2-2 and A4-3.\n12. **A6-0d** enumerate/delete ref pins and create/verify the off-repo backup bundle after A6-0c.\n13. **A6-1** execute the reclaim last, only after A1-A5 and A6-0a..0d are closed and Epic B's B6\n    is closed.\n\n### Observable rollout gates\n\n**A2-2 may not merge** until A2-1 has been merged to `main` for at least 24 hours and a completed\n`reconcile-bridge.yml` run has a `github.sha` that is a descendant of the A2-1 merge commit. Record\nthe A2-1 merge SHA, workflow run id, and `git merge-base --is-ancestor` result on A2-2 before merge.\nThis is the concrete writer-rollout signal; no pass-record version stamp exists.\n\n**A6-1 may not begin** until A6-0a has been merged to `main` for at least 24 hours and the same\ndescendant-SHA workflow evidence is recorded, because older binaries ignore the epoch field.\nThe operator-attested zero-session/MCP-stop and bundle requirements remain additional gates.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThree committed-format changes share one store file. A2-1 is reversible because it continues\nwriting the legacy field. A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes\nidempotently. A2-2 and A4-2 are irreversible expand/contract steps: A2-2 requires the explicit\n24-hour descendant-workflow gate above; A4-2 requires both the forward full->key-set corpus diff\nand the reverse key-set->full rollback diff before merge. The epoch value is introduced only by\nthe reclaim commit, after the new reader is deployed.\n\nPost-publish rollback is an explicit second quiesced window, not an application-level union:\n\n1. Disable both reconciler workflows, pause the review-bot/autodeploy writers, poll for no in-flight\n   runs and an empty Gerrit review queue, and obtain the operator's zero-session/stopped-MCP\n   confirmation again.\n2. Verify the off-repo bundle, unbundle it into a fresh unfiltered scratch clone, and verify that\n   the recorded old tip and deleted tag tips resolve exactly.\n3. Restore the old `tickets` tip with `--force-with-lease=<rewritten-tip>:<old-tip>`. This direct,\n   operator-controlled ref replacement does not run the application merge guards. Never bypass\n   an epoch mismatch inside `sync._union_merge` or `push.py`.\n4. Reset/reclone every writer (shared local tracker, review-bot EBS clone, and ephemeral workflow\n   worktrees) to the restored tip before re-enabling writes. New-epoch clones must be replaced;\n   their mismatch refusal is the safety signal, not a condition to override.\n5. Re-run tree/count/identity checks, then re-enable writers in the same order as the forward path.\n\nThis makes the bundle executable as recovery while preserving fail-closed behavior in ordinary\nclients. A6 remains intentionally non-resumable; all graph assertions run on the scratch clone\nbefore either forward or rollback publication.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Marginal packed cost per changed `bindings.json` version is **<=25% of the pre-change\n      baseline measured by the same method** (N>=40 consecutive revisions in a clean repo,\n      repack `--window=250 --depth=50`, compute `(pack_N - pack_1)/(N-1)`). Baseline: 12.79 KB.\n- [ ] Two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state produce byte-identical\n      `bindings.json` and create no commit. Tier: stateful integration asserting bytes and commits.\n- [ ] `baseline_advanced_at` is absent from every entry written by `set_baseline`, and no `src/`\n      reference remains.\n- [ ] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves the worktree byte-identical.\n- [ ] A dict-shaped baseline through live `compute_update_fields` matches its normalized-string\n      equivalent, and stored description/status/priority are scalars while assignee stays raw.\n- [ ] Full-prev versus key-set-prev corpus mutation diff over >=4 real snapshot pairs has zero\n      delta in non-empty effects reaching Jira; the reverse-direction diff is recorded too.\n- [ ] `outbound_differ.py` remains <=800 LOC under the locked module-size gate.\n- [ ] A fresh unfiltered `tickets` clone is <=150 MB; rewritten `HEAD^{tree}` equals the recorded\n      pre-rewrite tip tree after the dynamic re-add; commit and merge counts are unchanged.\n- [ ] Before publication, a synthetic post-rewrite writer test in temporary real clones pushes a\n      representative review-bot ticket commit, then proves `merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip>\n      <new-tip>` is false and incremental `size-pack` growth is <1 MB. Tier: repo integration.\n- [ ] After the first real post-window review-bot write, the same ancestry and size checks are\n      recorded as a ticket comment with old tip, new tip, Gerrit change/vote identifier, command\n      exits, and measured byte growth. **[operator-attested post-deploy observation]**\n- [ ] A stale-epoch clone aborts without a merge at both `sync._union_merge` and `push.py`'s non-FF\n      retry, including the complete absent/present/corrupt epoch matrix and operator-visible log.\n- [ ] The ADR enumerates all format changes, mixed-version protocol, A2-2 gate, and rollback limits.\n- [ ] The off-repo backup bundle exists and `git bundle verify` passes. **[operator-attested]**\n- [ ] Operator confirms zero active sessions and all `rebar-mcp` servers stopped before the\n      reclaim window. **[operator-attested]**"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785689191807638001,"uuid":"8a088405-ad3e-48b8-9f39-e580ffe18a46"}